{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Queuing the probe built and locally verified for the child admission question's registered discriminator. It measures the two remaining halves: whether the node with an empty configuration campaigns on its own, and whether it accepts an outsider's AppendEntries and takes that non-member as its leader. A setup event was added so the setup and the results are separate emissions.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"s-runfollower\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":155,\\\"end_line\\\":260,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}\n ],\n \\\"experiment\\\":{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"7e10640e7212486b94a80f04b69febc2-question-1\\\",\n  \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-runfollower\\\",\\\"s-appendentries-stage\\\",\\\"s-restore-committed\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A single-node in-memory cluster with a commit-tracking store and RestoreCommittedLogs enabled is restarted from its own stores so its configuration is empty; the node is then watched over several heartbeat timeouts for any campaign of its own, after which an outsider reachable through the transport sends one AppendEntries request with a higher term and no entries, and the node's state, its leader identity and the response are recorded.\\\",\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n    \\\"Cluster, transport, log store and FSM are the repository's own MakeClusterCustom, InmemTransport, InmemCommitTrackingStore and MockFSM facilities.\\\",\n    \\\"Snapshotting is disabled by configuration so the restarted node's configuration is empty rather than stale.\\\",\n    \\\"The outsider is a server that appears in no configuration the node holds; it is wired to the node's transport for the duration of the probe.\\\",\n    \\\"The AppendEntries request carries no entries, so accepting it only means accepting the sender as leader.\\\"\n   ]\n  },\n  \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Bootstrap a one-node cluster with RestoreCommittedLogs and commit-tracking stores, apply five commands, shut the node down, restart it with NewRaft on a fresh transport and emit the setup event with the live configuration length and whether the node is in its own configuration; sleep six heartbeat timeouts and record the node's state and any leader it knows; wire an outsider transport, send AppendEntries from the outsider with term+1, no entries and commit index 0, then emit the result event with the response success, the response term, the leader the node now reports and whether the outsider became that leader.\\\",\n  \\\"requirement\\\":\\\"A node that recovers from its own log must not accept a server outside the configuration it recorded as its leader, and its own election gating must stay consistent with the configuration it holds.\\\",\n  \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"Raft itself: appendEntries decides whose leadership to record and the follower loop decides when the node campaigns, both from the configuration the node recovered.\\\",\n  \\\"anchors\\\":[\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-appendentries-stage\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"appendEntries\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1458,\\\"end_line\\\":1458},\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-runfollower\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"runFollower\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":159,\\\"end_line\\\":159}\n  ],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n   {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"empty-config-leader-setup\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"empty_config_leader_setup\\\",\n    \\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"live_config_len\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0},\n                  {\\\"field\\\":\\\"node_in_own_config\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False}]}\n  ],\n  \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"empty_config_leader_admission\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"variant\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"empty-config-leader-setup\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"outsider_became_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"A server outside the node's configuration does not become the node's leader.\\\"},\n   {\\\"event\\\":\\\"empty_config_leader_admission\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"variant\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"empty-config-leader-setup\\\",\n    \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"node_campaigned_on_its_own\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n    \\\"description\\\":\\\"The node does not start an election of its own while its configuration is empty.\\\"}\n  ]\n }\n}\njson.dump(u,open('update.json','w'),indent=2); print('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
